# Environment and Config Rules

## Never hardcode
Never hardcode API URLs, Supabase URLs, API keys, or model names in route handlers or components.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const supabase = createClient('https://xyz.supabase.co', 'eyJ...')

// ✅ GOOD
const supabase = createClient(
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
)
```

## Environment variable rules
- Secrets live in `.env.local` (gitignored) or Vercel dashboard — never in source code
- `.env.example` is the only env file committed to git — no real values, ever
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix only for variables that must be readable in the browser
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` is server-only — never use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` on it

## AI model name
The Anthropic model name is a constant in `lib/ai/generate.ts`. Never scatter it across files.

```typescript
// lib/ai/generate.ts
const MODEL = 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022'
```

## Adding new environment variables
1. Add to `.env.local` locally
2. Add to `.env.example` with an empty value and a comment
3. Add to Vercel dashboard for production
4. Never create new `.env` files beyond `.env.local` and `.env.example`
